Offer a drag to the window system

gpui carries a drag to its own views, and hands the window system only a
drag of files, once the pointer leaves the window, so nothing outside the
window a gesture started in hears of any other drag, and nothing it draws
is reachable past that window's edge. Give a window the
requests to offer a gesture to the window system, to say which mime type
it takes a drag under, and to hear what a drag the window system carries
does; a backend that implements none of them takes no gesture and says
so. Rasterizing a glyph goes with them: what a window system draws for a
drag is an image, and gpui's text system is where the application's own
faces are loaded.

